    "title": "Driver suspected of DUI arrested, passenger dead in SR-54 crash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Domenick Candelieri ,\n1 hours ago\nSAN DIEGO (FOX 5/KUSI) — A driver was arrested and a passenger died in a suspected driving under the influence (DUI) crash Wednesday on State Route 54.\nThe incident occurred around 12:54 a.m. on SR-54 eastbound, located east of Highland Avenue, the California Highway Patrol said in a news release.\nAuthorities say a 20-year-old man was driving a white Nissan with a 21-year-old passenger when for unknown reasons the vehicle veered off the road into a reverse gore point, struck a stationary sign and traveled down a dirt embankment.\nSuspect arrested after man found shot to death inside Ramona home The 21-year-old woman was taken to the hospital where she died from her injuries, per CHP.\nThe driver was arrested on suspicion of DUI.\nAnyone who witnessed the crash is asked to contact the CHP San Diego Area directly at 858-293-6000.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to FOX 5 San Diego & KUSI News.",
